lvr2 Debian packaging notes
==========================

The ROS and CMake package identity is now lvr3, so Debian builds install
`package.xml` under `share/lvr3` and provide the self-contained lvr3 CMake
package. The Debian source and binary package names intentionally preserve the
existing lvr2 identities as a compatibility surface until a separate Debian
rename slice is accepted.

Distributor builds use system packages instead of the default vcpkg-first
workflow by passing `-DLVR2_WITH_VCPKG=OFF`. Mesh asset I/O uses the required
private Assimp backend and is packaged as shared-only, so both Debian configure
paths pass `-DBUILD_SHARED_LIBS=ON -DLVR2_BUILD_STATIC_LIBS=OFF`.

The current Ubuntu/ROS dependency set has verified package or rosdep names for
Assimp (`libassimp-dev` / `assimp`), tl-expected (`libexpected-dev`), spdlog
(`libspdlog-dev` / `spdlog`), and the existing system dependencies such as TBB,
TIFF, GDAL, HDF5, OpenCV, Eigen, YAML-CPP, OpenGL/GLUT, and OpenCL.

The package-backed CMake build also requires HighFive, rply, and LASlib/LAStools.
Verified Lyrical/Resolute Debian package names and rosdep keys for those dependencies
are not recorded here yet, so they are deliberately not listed as Debian or ROS
package dependencies. Full Debian builds may remain blocked on those packages
until distro packaging or local rosdep rules provide them.
